  ## Packaging a tool with flakes

  None of the code blocks below say
  what language they are in, as is
  common with static site generators
  that drop the class.

                                      
    { pkgs, lib, ... }:               
    {                                 
      environment.systemPackages = …  
      services.openssh.enable = tru…  
      programs.fish.enable = lib.mk…  
    }                                 
                                      

  Build it with:

                                      
    nix build .#default --no-link     
                                      

  The package itself:

                                      
    {                                 
      lib,                            
      buildGoModule,                  
    }:                                
    buildGoModule {                   
      pname = "izrss";                
      version = "0.4.0";              
      src = ./.;                      
      vendorHash = lib.fakeHash;      
      ldflags = [ "-s" "-w" ];        
      meta.mainProgram = "izrss";     
    }                                 
                                      

  A shell script that wraps it:

                                      
    #!/usr/bin/env bash               
    set -euo pipefail                 
    for f in "$@"; do                 
      echo "building $f"              
    done                              
                                      

  And the secrets file, which is YAML:

                                      
    keys:                             
      - &isabel age1qyqszqgpqyqszqg…  
    creation_rules:                   
      - path_regex: secrets/[^/]+\.…  
                                      

  Plain output is left alone:

                                      
    hello world, this is just some …  
    from a command that ran           
                                      